  "hypothesis": "On the reloaded 90 MHz B40 image the device graph makespan of three frozen anchors (streaming HBM, compute-bound medium GEMM, multi-launch HBM decode) is stable across independent sessions, so single qualification records of long device tasks are admissible for Stage 1 board comparisons.",
  "competing_explanations": [
    "image or clock differs from B40-OBS (checked by identity, not by timing)",
    "buffer placement or residual device state from earlier processes changes cycles (R40-01 tiny points)",
    "host submission gaps enter the graph makespan of the multi-launch decode",
    "thermal or shared-card interference"
  ],
  "expected_counter_changes": [
    "no counter change: identical code and configuration in every session",
    "serial-grid and graph-makespan spread across the 3 sessions small relative to R41 A/B effects",
    "decode graph makespan exceeds its serial-grid sum only by submission gaps"
  ],
  "expected_observations": [
    "3 anchors x 3 independent sessions pass numerically without fallback on image a88ebdf5 at 90 MHz",
    "per-anchor relative spread of graph makespan recorded in batch.json samples"
  ],
